Package: clusterLibreville
Title: Parallel and Deterministic Leiden Community Detection
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: person("btraven", email = "ben.uzh@proton.me", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A parallel and deterministic implementation of the Leiden
    community detection algorithm (Traag, Waltman and van Eck 2019,
    <doi:10.1038/s41598-019-41695-z>) for large sparse graphs such as
    single-cell kNN and SNN graphs, implemented in Rust. The
    same seed gives the same labels at any number of threads. The parallel
    design follows GVE-Leiden (Sahu 2023, <arXiv:2312.13936>). Works on
    sparse matrices, Seurat graphs and igraph graphs, and as a bluster
    clustering function.
